{"author":{"id":"b409816c5cd5ab140d1d52eb33aace35de44952bb794b19806fd57f6ecb1ace9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1789858274,"nonce":"5qo0YgxSrkxCyYBEvE+X1+UHRFo=","title":"CSE rewrote a phi's block instead of its value when a substituted instruction fed the phi","message":"cse::apply_substitutions walked phi incomings as (block, value) where HirPhi::incoming is (value, block): the block id went through the substitution map (a no-op) and the value kept naming the instruction remove_redundant_instructions then dropped. A loop-carried increment that CSE found redundant, such as the width doubling in the builtins' merge sort once two constant 2s were one value, left the header phi reading a value nothing defines: the interpreter failed with \"type mismatch: expected integer, got Undef\", compiled code read garbage. sign_fold's select picks went through the same path.\n\napply_substitutions now rewrites the value element of each incoming and uses HirInstruction::replace_uses / for_each_operand for the rest, which know every variant, instead of its own match with a silent catch-all. ZYNTAX_CHECK_HIR_USES=1 runs a definedness check after each pass of the sweep and names the pass that broke it.","files":null}]}